ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE PREDICTION SYSTEM


1. PROJECT DESCRIPTION :-
The Academic Performance Prediction project is a simple Python console
application that can predict a student’s academic performance.

 It will calculate a student’s
performance score based on his attendance, average study hours, previous
exam marks, assignment submission, and internal marks.


Once the score has been calculated, the student’s performance will be predicted
as excellent, good, average, and needs improvement.


2. FEATURES :-
It has the following features:
1. Take student details as input


2. Calculate the performance score
3. Convert the study hours into percentage
4. Limit the score to 100%
5. Predict the performance result
6. Display performance related message
7. Provide suggestions based on low scoring criteria
8. Works in Python console


3. INPUTS :-
The following inputs will be provided:
1. Student Name
2. Attendance Percentage
3. Average Study Hours Per Day
4. Previous Exam Marks Percentage
5. Assignment Completion Percentage
6. Internal Marks Percentage
4. WEIGHTAGE USED :-
The student’s performance will be calculated using the following formula:
Score = Attendance 0.2 + Study Hours % 0.15 + Previous Marks 0.25 + Assignment % 0.15 + Internal Marks 0.25
Where the study hours percentage is calculated as study hours / 8 100.
Using the calculated score, the student’s performance is predicted using the following ranges:
Score >= 85
Excellent
Score >= 70 and < 85
Good
Score >= 55 and < 70
Average
Score < 55
Needs Improvement


5. SUGGESTION SYSTEM :-
According to the inputs, the following suggestions will be made.
If attendance is less than 75%,
then improve the class attendance.
If study hours per day is less than 3 hours,
increase the average study hours.
If previous exam marks percentage is less than 60%,
focus more on improving the previous exam score.
If assignment completion percentage is less than 70%,
complete the assignments regularly.
If internal marks percentage is less than 60%,
focus more on improving the internal assessment score.
Otherwise, keep up the good work!


6. TECHNOLOGIES USED :-
PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE-Python 3
LIBRARIES-None
REQUIREMENTS
1. Python 3
2. Any operating system that supports Python
3. Terminal, VS Code, PyCharm, or any other Python IDE


7. HOW TO RUN :-
1. Install Python 3 if it is not already installed.
2. Save the program in a file with the following name:
academic_performance.py
3. Open a terminal in the project folder.
4. Run the following command:


python academic_performance.py
5. Enter the student details when prompted.
6. It will display the result, message, and suggestions.
